13: Method getValue() declares no return type while Lib\Control::getValue() returns mixed, which the body may not return
20: Method getItems() returns iterable while Lib\Control::getItems() returns array, which the body may not return
27: Method render() lacks the parameter $attrs that Lib\Control::render() declares
27: Method render() lacks the parameter $strict that Lib\Control::render() declares
37: Parameter $val of setValue() takes string while that of Lib\Control::setValue() takes mixed
37: Parameter $val of setValue() is named $value in Lib\Control::setValue(), which a caller passing it by name notices
45: Method attach() is protected while Lib\Control::attach() is public
51: Method getName() overrides the final Lib\Control::getName()
61: Parameter $file of load() is named $name in Lib\Loader::load(), but the body names a variable indirectly
